"""
Qualitative analysis for the SLAKE-finetuned Q-FSRU checkpoint.

Fixes the duplicate-example bug present in the previous version: the same
image-question pair could appear in both the "case study" (FSRU helps) and
"failure case" (FSRU hurts) figures, because each figure ran its own
independent decode() calls over the model. Two separate forward passes are
not guaranteed to be bit-identical on GPU (cuDNN algorithm selection, TF32
matmuls, and non-deterministic reduction order in attention/convolution
kernels can all perturb logits by a tiny amount), so a borderline example
could be scored "correct" in one pass and "incorrect" in the other, letting
it satisfy both the success predicate and the failure predicate across the
two separate runs.

The fix: run inference exactly ONCE per example, cache predictions keyed by
a stable id, and partition that single cache into disjoint success/failure
sets. Determinism flags are also set explicitly so repeated full runs of
this script reproduce the same figures.
"""

import os
import textwrap
import numpy as np
import torch
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt


